    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-83371-8_3",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-030-83371-8_3",
      "title": "SmartCities. Technology as Enabler",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "José A. Ondiviela"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2021,
      "abstract": "An evaluation of the SmartCity concept is described since its first conception, too much linked to technology to monitor and control the physical components of a city, towards latest human perspective, placing the citizen services and the citizen active participation as a must-have design principle. Technology is always present, as enabler, as the perfect catalyzer of city prosperity. Also, its role is evolving from a core destination to a tool, omnipresent, indispensable, but a tool, a mean. Different definitions and approaches, how-to models, stages in this evolution, and finally, the humanization of Smartcities and its implications will be studied.",
