    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-981-99-0264-4_43",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-981-99-0264-4_43",
      "title": "Method for the Transfer and Further Development of Document-Based Data and Information in a Model-Based Development Environment Using the Example of a Small Mission Satellite",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Emir Gadzo, Jan Mehlstäubl, ... Kristin Paetzold"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2023,
      "abstract": "In today’s projects, the system of the individual satellite is no longer the single decisive development objective. The focus of the development goal is on the services and performance of the emerging network, consisting of different systems that interact and collaborate in a multidisciplinary manner. They form a network that can meet the needs and desires of the users while considering the interests of the operators. To ensure the successful development of such a system of systems, it is necessary to use efficient, goal-oriented, powerful, and above all, systematic approaches in the product development process when developing the individual systems. This paper presents the groundwork for a new model-based method for the systematic identification of gaps, inconsistencies, and incompleteness in existing data, generated in a document-based approach within the development process of a small mission satellite. The fundamentals of MBSE serve as a basis and guideline in the conceptual design and provide the necessary tools for the realization and implementation of a target-oriented approach. Initial validation of the approach was performed using an experimental payload unit of the small satellite. The experimental unit, consisting of several payload components, was defined as the system of interest. This system of interest in turn operates in a system context systematically developed by the model-based method.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "In today’s projects, the system of the individual satellite is no longer the single decisive development objective. The focus of the development goal...",
      "citationCount": 0,
      "openAccess_pdf": {},
      "url": "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-99-0264-4_43",
      "source": "Springer Nature Link",
      "rank": 62,
      "publicationTitle": "Design in the Era of Industry 4.0, Volume 2",
      "publicationDate": "2023",
      "publicationDateSourceTag": "Springer rendered search-result Date published",
