    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-24310-2_7",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-3-032-24310-2_7",
      "title": "Simulation and Evaluation of 6G Non-terrestrial Networks",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Haibo Zhou, Xin Zhang, Weihua Zhuang"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2026,
      "abstract": "Having thoroughly explored the foundational concepts, architectural designs, physical layer optimizations, access management strategies, routing and transmission mechanisms, and resource management techniques for 6G NTNs in the preceding chapters, it becomes imperative to rigorously evaluate and validate the performance of these complex systems. The theoretical advancements and proposed solutions, while promising, require robust assessment under realistic conditions to ascertain their practical feasibility and efficiency. This necessity is further compounded by highly dynamic nature of network topologies and the large scale of emerging mega-constellations, which impose significant challenges on accurate constellation modeling and reliable performance evaluation. To address these critical challenges, this chapter is dedicated to introducing and detailing UltraStar, a novel high-fidelity and high-efficiency computer simulator specifically designed to support the development and rigorous evaluation of 6G wireless communication systems utilizing ultradense mega-constellation scenario of 6G NTN. We will comprehensively present UltraStar’s architecture, functionalities, and its unique capabilities for accurately modeling the intricate dynamics, large scale, and heterogeneous characteristics inherent to NTN environments. Effective simulation, particularly through advanced tools like UltraStar, is indispensable for understanding system behavior, identifying potential bottlenecks, optimizing design parameters, and demonstrating the efficacy of various algorithms and protocols before actual deployment, thereby paving the way for the successful realization of these advanced communication paradigms.",
      "abstract_not_available": false,
      "snippet": "Having thoroughly explored the foundational concepts, architectural designs, physical layer optimizations, access management strategies, routing and...",
      "citationCount": 0,
